Id: lin053w
Severity: WARN
Category: network
Check: check_network_config
Fix: Stop the multicast routing daemon (pimd, smcroute, mrouted) unless this host is a multicast router.
References: Linux kernel networking documentation (ip-sysctl, mc_forwarding)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST SC-5, SC-7; ISO 8.20; CE Secure configuration

The host routes multicast traffic between its interfaces:
net.ipv4.conf.all.mc_forwarding is 1. The flag is read-only to
sysctl; only a multicast routing daemon (pimd, smcroute, mrouted)
turns it on, so one is or was running here. A host that is not meant
to be a router should forward nothing (lin015w covers unicast), and a
routing daemon is a network service with an attack surface of its
own. The flag is the running kernel's, so an offline root (--root) is
not judged.
